      <tei:div type="colophon" subtype="introduction">
        <tei:p>This tefillah is a Yizkor honoring the Taíno Nation and all other Indigenous Americans who were wiped out by Christopher Columbus. It is meant to be said on Indigenous People’s day/Columbus Day. It talks about the suffering the people of America were subjected too and is a prayer asking H-shem to both care for them in death and to tell the whole world what happened.</tei:p>
      </tei:div>
      <j:endConditional target="#osp_69464_introduction"/>
